                        "source_entry_id": "9136e04e-ea61-3dc3-a4e9-fd809c6950aa",
                        "source_sense_id": "ebe8c6bb-774f-379b-9ce1-7a7de0b09038",
                        "target_lang_word": "hydrochloride",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hydrochloride",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1aa195c3-c452-31a1-a35a-15c761614d82",
                                        "entry_id": "3fe89815-dbd6-3c33-9599-5c1765334bec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A compound of hydrochloric acid with an organic base such as an amine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f18ba8fb-9d45-45af-bc11-425b68e0368c",
                                                "sense_id": "1aa195c3-c452-31a1-a35a-15c761614d82",
                                                "text": "In contrast, a water-repellent substance, for example, fluoric resin or Teflon, is extremely nonaffinitive with the oily oxime hydrochlorides and has a nature to repel it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e04371ca-3509-4605-a8ec-3ca3b20ac026",
                                                "sense_id": "1aa195c3-c452-31a1-a35a-15c761614d82",
                                                "text": "After 15, 30, 60 or 90 days, the animals (n = 5 per time point for each subgroup) were sacrificed via an overdose of ketamine and xylazine hydrochloride (Vetbrands Brazil Limited, Jacareí, SP), and the hemimaxillae were removed and fixed in 10% formalin solution (Fig 1 )."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9e75fb77-3da8-4e1e-a4c1-99563c3334d1",
                        "source_entry_id": "9136e04e-ea61-3dc3-a4e9-fd809c6950aa",
                        "source_sense_id": "ebe8c6bb-774f-379b-9ce1-7a7de0b09038",
                        "target_lang_word": "chlorhydrate",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chlorhydrate",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bdff0c67-80b6-3147-a28d-7c6062725f4b",
                                        "entry_id": "e6b27d0e-0a71-3d7e-b18c-72cc4b0a739f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sel formé par la combinaison de l’acide chlorhydrique avec certaines bases."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d859f585-7290-4b32-b29d-a5d3d3bab698",
                                                "sense_id": "bdff0c67-80b6-3147-a28d-7c6062725f4b",
                                                "text": "On retire la morphine de l'extrait d'opium au moyen d’un lait de chaux qui dissout la morphine sous forme de morphinate ; l'addition de chlorhydrate d'ammoniaque précipite la morphine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4d0638d-9739-413f-abe2-dfeaf1a04234",
                                                "sense_id": "bdff0c67-80b6-3147-a28d-7c6062725f4b",
                                                "text": "Le chlorhydrate est utilisé pour les injections retard (à forme prolongée) contrairement à l'acétate, qui est utilisée aussi pour les injections retard mais à forme semi prolongée."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08f9e89c-8cd1-4961-b9fe-d5406f1c628c",
                                                "sense_id": "bdff0c67-80b6-3147-a28d-7c6062725f4b",
                                                "text": "Il espérait pouvoir ainsi utiliser les chlorhydrates de ces dérivés qui seraient forcément hydrosolubles."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
